0:[$0000FF]KamStar - Overthrow
1:KSU %d
2:[$00CE72]Season I - KamStar Beginning |[$0000FF]Season II - KamStar Fall |[$00CE72]Season III - KamStar Nemesis Part 1 |[$00CE72]Season III - KamStar Nemesis Part 2 [$FFFFFF] | |Thirteen years have passed since the civil war in Artidram. All the kingdoms of this continent live in harmony and peace. However, there is always a factor that can disturb this peace. ||The campaign has many dialogues and cinematic scenes that can be sped up. ||I recommend playing the first part of the KamStar story, titled: KamStar - Beginning ||Author: KingDyron |Scenario: MEMGOR
10:The Power of Hanrain||[$FFB1B9]King Dyron[$ffffff]: All the kingdoms of Ardidram live in peace with each other. In the event of a greater external threat or a rebellion by one of the rulers of Ardidram, all the other kingdoms will come to the defense of the continent. The people of Distillion ceased their attacks ten years ago, and for some time now we have been attacked by the indomitable King Teryton. Hanrain is the main attacker, for reasons still unknown to me.
11:-cutscene-|The Pact||[$FFB1B9]King Dyron[$ffffff]: King Teryton's constant attacks are becoming tiresome. We must do something about it.
12:"Guest"||Malcolm: King Ratling has set out for the Valtarian garrison. The steward remains in power, and I wanted to stay and explore Valtarian Castle. Because what harm could there be in the world if there's no war? :5_00155
13:Through the Desert||Malcolm: Could someone enlighten me on what's going on here? Why did Dyron enter Valtaria and start murdering everyone around him? Of course, it's not Dyron, but he has his armor and axes. Plus... He let me just leave:5_00145. Me??? A coward:5_00146??? Well, we start the week with violence:5_00145. King Drein... I hope he knows what to do. We're on our way.
14:The Stronghold||Malcolm: They've led us into the castle of Nir Stronghold. Now we just have to talk to the king.
15:-cutscene-|News||Malcolm: After this attack, the king will surely realize something is wrong.
16:Desolation of Souls||Malcolm: Drein's spies have returned from Valtaria. Kregor isn't taking over the surrounding villages, he's destroying them. Furthermore, he regularly assaults the Valtarian garrison and Andaro. As for the mysterious enemy, we know nothing. And the Black Inquisition is now called the Grand Inquisition, not much difference. Also, I almost forgot. Kregor has sent an army from Valtaria to Hanrain. We have to stop it.
17:-cutscene-|Ruined Kingdom||Malcolm: I see Hanrain will be in for a snowstorm. Clouds blacker than the ground after rain. No... It's smoke:5_00144... So Milo was right. Something terrible has happened in the north. Milo said Dyron has returned to his city. I need to talk to him. At first glance, I thought Dyron was dead, but thankfully, he's not.
18:-cutscene-|Plan of Action||Malcolm: Just relay this news to Drein and we can move on.
19:Entrance to the Tunnel||Malcolm: I never thought I'd say this, but I'm not entirely happy about it. Ehh:5_00157Yeah, right. Drein didn't mention any difficulties before the tunnel. Apparently, the Grand Inquisition has already taken it over. Let's just hope they don't get too far.
20:Tunnel Part 1||Malcolm: They want to destroy Citland from within. I know King Alan isn't a very nice guy, but even he shouldn't suffer such a fate.
21:Tunnel Part 2||Malcolm: Now we'd better expand. We have a suitable cave to build in. Build, build, gentlemen.|||I know... Building in tunnels is a bit of a stretch, but you have to deal with it somehow. Deal with it.
22:Tunnel Part 3||Malcolm: The journey continues, I should have taken provisions for the journey:4_00364:4_00361
23:Tribe of Destillion||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: I'm on Darin, more specifically in the part where the Destillion people live. I didn't think I'd be visiting them so soon. Especially after their last encounter. However, protecting the world is more important. I need to find Iris, and as soon as possible.
24:Citland Entrance||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: I'm still alive. So it's good. Unfortunately, or fortunately, the fortune teller isn't here. I'll have to wait for her. I hope Malcolm is doing much better.|Malcolm: Everything's fine with me:5_00141
25:Island City||Malcolm: Mmmm... That's good chicken... I haven't had one like that in ages... Oh... Sorry... Back to the main story...|Yessss! Victory:5_00141 And how spectacular. There's Alan:5_00154, there's Iris:5_00132 and there's:5_00136 ... How was she:5_00155... Attila, right:5_00151. Now we just have to retake the city from the scoundrels and we can move on with our story:5_00150
26:-cutscene-|Meeting||Malcolm: We're at Alan's castle and I have to admit, it's quite grand:5_00143 It's so beautifully decorated here:5_00136 Flowers here, deciduous and coniferous trees there, spaced perfectly apart:5_00140 It's as if I were building it:5_00154 But this is no time for admiring, we need to discuss what's next:5_00140 The longer we fight, the stronger the enemy becomes.
27:-cutscene-|Darin Continent||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: The fortune teller has finally arrived and pardoned me for trespassing on Distillon's grounds. Hopefully, she'll help me find a way to defeat "The Guest"
28:The Power of Andaro||Malcolm: Andaro:5_00132, Andaro:5_00141. We'll be in Andaro:5_00151, nana na na. Wow, I'm singing today, boys:5_00135
29:The Power of Nir Stronghold||[$CC00C0]King Drein[$FFFFFF]: Unfortunately, Malcolm didn't manage to save Andaro in time. It was attacked by a guy with an axe. We wouldn't have stood a chance against him anyway. But we must press on. We must gather an army, as Dyron planned. Hopefully, he will succeed in convincing Distillion's family to fight.
30:The Power of Circlet Stronghold||Baron Ari: An army to fight the mysterious "Guest." I don't know if it's the best idea, but an order is an order.
31:The Power of the Garrison||[$FFDB33]King Ratling[$FFFFFF]: I've had enough of this war. If it's not Kregor, then it's "Guest" with an axe. And it was so peaceful here. The signal tower in Nir Stronghold is already burning. I have to hurry. The constant attacks are preventing me from recruiting enough troops.
32:After the answers||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: Before Iris left, she gave me her bracelet. She claims that thanks to it, I will instantly return to the teleportation ring. Interesting technology. However, I won't let them just take her away. I intend to free her. I am in the southern part of Darin. This is where the mysterious commander with the gauntlet brought Iris. However, there is a well-protected city here and you will have to go unnoticed, but where... We will have to check every corner.
33:Truth's Labyrinth Part 1||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: They killed her... Everyone I lost... They must be avenged. I know where the labyrinth of death is. It's where the second gauntlet of existence, the gauntlet of destruction, is supposed to be. At the bottom of the ocean, between Darin, Revelia, and Artidram. I should get there with the diving bell. I'm leaving immediately.
34:Truth's Labyrinth Part 2||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: The second part of the labyrinth. Traps at every corner... People were going mad here. At least that's what Father told me.
35:-cutscene-|Assault on Valtaria||Malcolm: I have bad news:5_00133 King Ratling was attacked by "The Guest." He killed the king and took over his army. But we must continue. We are all here. Together. We are storming Valtaria.
36:-cutscene-|Change of Power||Malcolm:Unbelievable. We were supposed to assault Valtaria, but "The Guest" beat us to it. He destroyed the entire capital of Artidram and killed Kregor. What's going on here? Our entire plan has gone down the drain. What should we do?|[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Out of the way! I'll tell you what to do.
37:Garrison in front of the Volcano|Malcolm: From now on, Attila has taken command of my army, so here you go:5_00156|[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: Thank you, Malcolm. We're constantly pursuing the enemy. We have an army and ballistaa. When the final battle comes, "The Guest" will have to either surrender or die. 
38:-cutscene-|Support||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: The gauntlet is impressive. It works like my kinetic axe, but it has a drawback: it needs a recharge time. It's not long, but still. Fighting the enemy can be difficult. I'll return immediately. I left my boat on the shore of the Tribe of Distillion's village.
39:The Power of Irim||[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: It's much worse than I expected. The enemy doesn't intend to leave Artidram, they've hidden themselves in the volcano itself, good thing it's inactive. However, it will be difficult to get there. Only one large bridge and several smaller ones lead inside. This will be a really tough battle. The real war begins.|Malcolm: Relax, we have ballistas:5_00150|[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: You shouldn't build them.|Malcolm: After winning the battle, I will destroy them. I promise:5_00151
40:-cutscene-|Enemy defeated||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: The enemy is defeated. Now we will find out who my son's killer is. 
41:-cutscene-|It's not over yet||[$FFB1B9]Dyron[$ffffff]: We did it. It's unbelievable that after all this, our greatest enemy turned out to be a friend. Drein was right, you shouldn't trust anyone. Now let's get on with the plan to actually avenge Iris. Teth, get ready, I have an axe, a gauntlet, and plenty of support from my friends. Get ready, Teth, we're ready.
42:-cutscene-|Consequences||[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: You were supposed to destroy them! That will bring disaster.|Malcolm: Oh come on, you're exaggerating a bit:5_00151|[$09F641]Attilia[$ffffff]: This isn't a joke anymore, Malcolm...|Malcolm: What could possibly happen:5_00155? 
43: Congratulations! You've won all the missions in this campaign. The second part of the KamStar campaign series is complete. You've learned the story of the enemy who has long been planning to seize Dyron's armor. The world must rebuild itself once again, but it won't be easy, as the new enemy has already begun his activities. | The next installment will be based primarily on the story rather than the gameplay itself.
